-From dd284e537ffca0b3f50cf1d944d3eee04532e955 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
-From: Claude <claude@anthropic.com>
-Date: Sun, 26 Jul 2026 11:00:09 +0000
-Subject: [PATCH 1/2] Consolidate case/warranty demo seeders
-
-CaseManagementSeeder and CaseWarrantyDemoSeeder overlapped: both generated
-case rows, and running both would produce duplicate/conflicting demo data.
-CaseManagementSeeder wins on volume and per-case richness (factories, full
-status history, attachments), so it's kept as canonical and gains what
-CaseWarrantyDemoSeeder had that it didn't:
-
-- Cases now link to a real order/order_item/product for the customer when
-  one exists, instead of just customer_id.
-- Each case gets a crm_communication_logs row + short crm_chat_messages
-  thread, linked via ticket_id = case_number.
-
-CaseCommunicationLogSeeder is retired too, since it did the same
-comms/chat job as a separate pass over already-created cases -- running it
-after CaseManagementSeeder now would just be redundant.
-
-WarrantySeeder now links a claim's case_id to an existing case for the
-same customer (category Warranty/Product Defect, no claim yet) when one
-exists, mirroring what CaseController::store already does for real
-requests via the mock e-commerce trigger -- flagging a warranty issue
-there creates a case AND, if there's an eligible registration, a claim
-with case_id pointing at that case. A claim seeded this way also starts
-out assigned to whoever the linked case is assigned to.
-
-Note: WarrantySeeder now sets WarrantyClaim.assigned_to, which doesn't
-exist until the next commit's migration runs -- apply both before
-migrate:fresh.
